How can we use the nmap to detect the presents of a host-based-firewall or the presents of the filterying mechanism.
Nmap scanning methods in order to evade intrusion detection systems or in order to avoide triggering intrusion detection systems.
We perform nmap -sA Ack scanning option and


ACK scan is very usefull for detect how firewalls handle(处理) unexpected(非预期的) TCP packets.
Firewall: nmap -> ACK -> Target (In the case of no TCP 3-way-handshake -> Unusually)
No firewall: Target -> RST -> nmap (Denied to establish TCP session)

Stateful Firewall
nmap -> ACK -> Stateful Firewall -> Connection Tracking（连接跟踪）-> unexpected packet ->
Filtered -> No response... -> Nmap: Filtered

Connection tracking allows a firewall to evaluate incoming packets based on the state of previous communications.
The typically statefull firewall, saves a connection state table that records information, 
such as the source and destination IP addresses, ports, protocols, and connection states.
Client: 192.168.1.10:50000
Server: 192.168.1.100:80
Protocol: TCP
State: ESTABLISHED


Stateless Firewall
nmap -> ACK -> Stateless Firewall -> Check ACL rules -> If comply -> Target -> Nmap: Unfiltered
nmap -> ACK -> Stateless Firewall -> Check ACL rules -> No comply -> No response.. -> Nmap: Filtered



If port 80 enables to establish new connection while port 443 is filtered

1.
nmap -> SYN -> p80 -> OPEN
nmap -> ACK -> p80 -> Filtered
//The firewall allows the establishment of new session according to the tcp 3-way-handshake,
but is configured to filtered unexpected traffic (Ack)

2.
nmap -> SYN -> p80 -> OPEN
nmap -> ACK -> p80 -> Unfiltered
//The firewall allows both of the tcp SYN and ACK packet to pass throught

3.
nmap -> SYN -> p443 -> Filtered
nmap -> ACK -> p443 -> Unfiltered
//There may be a stateless filtering rule that specifically targets SYN packets.

4.
nmap -> SYN -> p443 -> Filtered
nmap -> ACK -> p443 -> Filtered
//Both of the tcp SYN and ACK scan is blokced and filtered by firewall, 
the firewall type cannot be determined.
